## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of a full retrieval pipeline, chunking strategy, and vector stores in a beginner-friendly way applicable to large-prod settings (Lyft/Discord/Adobe).

## Key Concepts

- Token-based chunking and overlap
- Local embeddings vs cloud APIs
- Vector databases and cosine similarity
- Data freshness and refresh strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal in-memory demo (no real model)
const chunks = [
  { text: 'chunk one', vec: [0.1,0.2,0.3] },
  { text: 'chunk two', vec: [0.0,0.2,0.4] }
];
function sim(a,b){ let dot = a.reduce((s,x,i)=> s + x*b[i],0); let na=Math.hypot(...a); let nb=Math.hypot(...b); return dot/(na*nb); }
const q=[0.08,0.18,0.28];
const top = chunks.map((c,i)=>({i, s: sim(c.vec,q)})).sort((A,B)=> B.s-A.s)[0];
console.log(top);
```

